{
"dur": 79.387,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.633,
"text": "Meanwhile, the hunt had stalled. Top cyber investigators were trying to crack the site's technology.",
"end": 6.908
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.908,
"vo_start": 7.183,
"vo_end": 11.663,
"text": "The breakthrough came from a tax investigator in New York: Gary Alford of the IRS.",
"end": 11.938
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 11.938,
"vo_start": 12.213,
"vo_end": 16.533,
"text": "His method was simple. He searched Google for the earliest mentions of Silk Road.",
"end": 16.808
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 16.808,
"vo_start": 17.083,
"vo_end": 24.123,
"text": "He found a post from January 2011 on a mushroom forum. A user called altoid was telling people about a new site called Silk Road.",
"end": 24.398
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 24.398,
"vo_start": 24.673,
"vo_end": 33.353,
"text": "Then the same username on a Bitcoin forum, in October 2011. Altoid was hiring a programmer, and said to email rossulbricht at gmail dot com.",
"end": 33.628
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 33.628,
"vo_start": 33.903,
"vo_end": 37.222,
"text": "A real name. The pirate's mask had cracked.",
"end": 37.497
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 37.497,
"vo_start": 37.772,
"vo_end": 45.689,
"text": "In July 2013, border officers seized a package from Canada with nine fake IDs, all with Ross's photo, addressed to his San Francisco home.",
"end": 45.964
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 45.964,
"vo_start": 46.239,
"vo_end": 53.039,
"text": "When Homeland Security agents knocked, he told them that, hypothetically, anyone could buy fake IDs on a site called Silk Road.",
"end": 53.314
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 53.314,
"vo_start": 53.589,
"vo_end": 58.869,
"text": "Around the same time, the FBI said a leak in the site's login page pointed to its server, in Iceland.",
"end": 59.144
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 59.144,
"vo_start": 59.419,
"vo_end": 64.897,
"text": "Investigators quietly copied it. How exactly they found it was later disputed in court.",
"end": 65.172
},
{
"i": 11,
"start": 65.172,
"vo_start": 65.447,
"vo_end": 73.287,
"text": "The server held chats, orders and accounts. They were sure they knew who Roberts was. Now they had to prove it.",
"end": 73.562
},
{
"i": 12,
"start": 73.562,
"vo_start": 73.837,
"vo_end": 78.437,
"text": "And his laptop was encrypted. If the lid closed, the evidence could be locked away for good.",
"end": 79.387
}
],
